 :context
 "ISIC Rev.5 6020 = television programming and broadcasting activities
  (licensed TV broadcast station operator). Live registry.edn :name for
  \"6020\" independently re-verified fresh: \"Television programming and
  broadcasting activities\", unambiguous, no truncation. UNLIKE most fleet
  targets, cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-6020 was NOT a fresh-scaffold
  404 -- gh api confirmed a PRE-EXISTING repo already at :blueprint tier
  (CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md/CONTRIBUTING.md/GOVERNANCE.md/LICENSE/README.md/
  SECURITY.md/blueprint.edn/docs/ only, from an earlier bulk-scaffolding
  pass, no deps.edn/src/test). This work ADDED the missing deps.edn/src/
  test module set on top of that existing boilerplate rather than
  re-scaffolding -- pre-existing docs kept and extended, not recreated.
  Pre-existing blueprint.edn already declared :itonami.blueprint/governor
  :broadcast-license-governor and :itonami.blueprint/id
  \"cloud-itonami-6020\" (no -isic- infix, unlike most sibling business-id
  shapes) -- both carried forward unchanged, already internally
  consistent. TV broadcasting touches editorial-content authority and
  emergency-alert-system decisions -- per ADR-2607152500's Wave4
  guardrail, closed op allowlist must never include an op that directly
  finalizes either; any 'flag concern' op always escalates, never
  auto-commit-eligible."

 :scope-exclusions
 ["finalizing an on-air-content decision (what actually airs, when, in what form) -- hard, permanent block"
  "finalizing an emergency-alert-broadcast decision (whether/when to trigger an Emergency Alert System transmission) -- hard, permanent block"
  "direct transmission dispatch, license-scope approval, billing-record publication without governor approval -- not represented in the closed op allowlist at all"]

 :self-trip-fix
 "Known bug class this batch repeatedly hit: bare-noun scope-excluded-terms
  (e.g. 'content', 'broadcast', 'emergency alert') self-match inside the
  mock advisor's own legitimate default rationale text, self-blocking the
  actor's happy path. Fix: scope-excluded-terms phrased as the
  finalization/execution ACTION ('finalize the on-air content decision',
  'authorize the emergency alert broadcast', JP equivalents), never a bare
  noun -- critical because :flag-content-concern's entire purpose is to
  discuss FCC-compliance/on-air-incident/emergency-alert topics using
  exactly those bare nouns. Dedicated regression test
  default-mock-advisor-proposals-never-self-trip-scope-exclusion in
  governor_test.clj asserts all 4 default proposal generators, for a
  clean registered+verified station, never trip :scope-excluded and never
  HARD-hold."

 :decision
 "Implement cloud-itonami-isic-6020 with Store/Advisor/Governor/Phase/
  Operation/Sim, mirroring cloud-itonami-isic-5913's filmdistops.* module
  shape module-for-module as tvbroadcastops.* (title/title-id renamed to
  station/station-id):
  - Store: Store protocol + MemStore, string-keyed stations directory
    (station-id/call-sign/name/registered?/verified?), append-only ledger
    + broadcast-log
  - Advisor: Advisor protocol + mock-advisor, 4 ops all :effect :propose --
    log-broadcast-record, schedule-broadcast-operation, flag-content-concern,
    coordinate-equipment-maintenance
  - Governor (BroadcastLicenseGovernor, matching pre-existing blueprint.edn's
    own declared governor name): 2 named HARD checks (station-unverified,
    effect-not-propose) + scope-exclusion/op-not-allowed folded check
    (finalize-on-air-content-decision / finalize-emergency-alert-broadcast-
    decision / closed 4-op allowlist). always-escalate-ops
    #{:flag-content-concern}, confidence-floor 0.6
  - Phase: 0->3 rollout (phase1 = log-broadcast-record only, approval;
    phase2 += schedule-broadcast-operation/coordinate-equipment-maintenance,
    approval; phase3 auto-commits those 3 when clean+confident;
    flag-content-concern never auto, any phase)
  - Operation: real langgraph-clj StateGraph (intake->advise->govern->decide
    ->commit|hold|request-approval), interrupt-before #{:request-approval},
    NOT a stub -- mirrors filmdistops.operation exactly
  - Sim: clojure -M:run demo, full happy path + always-escalate flow + all
    HARD-hold scenarios
  - Tests: store_contract_test, advisor_test, governor_test (incl. mandatory
    self-trip regression), phase_test, governor_contract_test -- 40 tests /
    119 assertions green
  - All .cljc portable, no JVM-only interop. AGPL-3.0-or-later. Pre-existing
    README/GOVERNANCE/CONTRIBUTING/SECURITY/CODE_OF_CONDUCT/blueprint.edn/
    docs kept as-is except an Implementation section appended to README.md
    and :itonami.blueprint/maturity :implemented added to blueprint.edn"

 :consequences
 {:positive
  ["ISIC 6020 TV-broadcasting-operations-coordination genuinely implemented
    and fully tested on top of a pre-existing blueprint-tier repo, without
    discarding or recreating its existing docs"
   "on-air-content-decision and emergency-alert-broadcast-decision
    exclusions hardcoded in governor checks (scope-exclusion-violations),
    not just README prose"
   "self-trip bug class fixed by construction (action-phrased terms) +
    covered by dedicated regression test, not avoided by luck"
   "flag-content-concern always-escalate is a two-layer invariant (governor
    always-escalate-ops + phase's permanent absence from every :auto set)"
   "portable .cljc, zero JVM-only constructs; clojure -M:lint 0 errors / 0 warnings"]
  :negative
  ["real persistent store (Datomic/kotoba-server) is a follow-up; tests use
    in-memory MemStore, matching every sibling actor's current maturity"
   "mock-advisor is deterministic, not a real LLM call; Advisor protocol seam
    ready for that swap but not wired in this ADR"]}

